From c3700a2834815368bc34aabf0e4bbc0c049add0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 18:19:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs(shepherd): reconcile State section with the local
 PR-monitor journal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CodeRabbit (minor): the State section claimed "no separate local state store",
which contradicts the durable per-PR NDJSON journal under
`.forge/pr-monitor/<repo>-<pr>/` documented above. Narrow the claim: the journal
(events.ndjson + snapshot + consumer cursors) IS the one local store — the
delivery/replay surface for `forge shepherd watch` / `events --since`; only the
bounded shepherd pass keeps no separate local state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/reference/shepherd.md | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/reference/shepherd.md b/docs/reference/shepherd.md
index 778e50b2..0149bbec 100644
--- a/docs/reference/shepherd.md
+++ b/docs/reference/shepherd.md
@@ -128,5 +128,8 @@ surface as every other rail.
 
 ## State
 
-Progress is durable in GitHub PR comments and labels plus `git`. There is no
-separate local state store.
+Progress is durable in GitHub PR comments and labels plus `git`. The one local
+store is the constant monitor's per-PR journal under
+`.forge/pr-monitor/<repo>-<pr>/` (the append-only `events.ndjson` + snapshot and
+consumer cursors) — the delivery/replay surface for `forge shepherd watch` and
+`events --since`. The bounded shepherd pass itself keeps no separate local state.
-- 
